  "overview": {
    "text": "Juliet Capulet is the young heroine of William Shakespeare’s tragedy Romeo and Juliet and the daughter of Lord and Lady Capulet. At a party hosted by her family, she meets Romeo, whose Montague family is locked in a feud with the Capulets; neither initially knows the other’s identity, but they fall in love. Juliet recognizes that Romeo’s family name makes him her enemy, yet questions whether a name defines a person, and the two arrange a secret marriage with Friar Lawrence. When her father pressures her to marry Count Paris, Juliet seeks the Friar’s help and takes a potion that makes her appear dead. A failed plan leads to both lovers’ deaths, which finally help end the feud.",
